# Structure

Mechanical file/dir SSOT (create/delete/move/split). Coding minimalism: `ponytail`. Ask-first list: `core`.

Use **Condition → Action → Verification**. **SRP ≠ one function per file** — extract only when the tables below say so, not for “cleanliness.”

## Add code

| Condition | Action | Verify |
| --- | --- | --- |
| Same type/role already in file | Merge | No duplicate defs |
| No same type + **2+** consumers | New file OK | All import it |
| No same type + **1** consumer | Inline | No new file |

Partial overlap → extend existing type; no parallel type.

## Add file

| Condition | Action | Verify |
| --- | --- | --- |
| Same role in target dir | Merge into that file | One file per role |
| No same role + 2+ consumers | Create | Consumers import path |
| No same role + 1 consumer | Do **not** create | Stay inline |

Before creating a file, confirm: ≥2 real consumers **or** framework layout requires it (e.g. Next `app/`). Hypothetical reuse does not count.

### Env / config (anti-wrapper)

Required env: validate at boot or config entry (fail fast). Call sites read that validated source — `process.env` where that is the app pattern, or a single boot-parsed config object (e.g. backend `env` from `getEnvConfig()`). Do **not** add one-off getter modules per variable.

| ❌ BAD | ✅ GOOD |
| --- | --- |
| `lib/api-internal-url.ts` with one `env ?? default` getter | Require `API_INTERNAL_URL` in `next.config.ts` / env types; `proxy` reads `process.env.API_INTERNAL_URL` |
| New file for a helper used once inside one service | Private method or inline in that service |
| One env var → one dedicated getter module | One boot config module grouping related settings (e.g. backend `src/lib/env.ts`); call sites import `env` |

## Delete

`grep` symbol/path first (**tests count**). Has refs → update callers, then delete. No refs → delete; clean barrels. Verify typecheck; no dangling imports.

## Split

Mixed unrelated concerns → split. Long but cohesive → **do not** split (not for line count).

## Move / promote shared

**2+** modules → shared location those consumers can import. **1** module → keep colocated. Never promote to `packages/*` for a hypothetical second consumer.

## Directories

**Flat is default.** Name by domain/concern (`kebab-case`), not artifact type (`components/cards/`, catch-all `utils/`).

| Would-be files | Action |
| --- | --- |
| 1–2 | Do not create dir; keep flat |
| 3+ | Create only with business/domain name |

Exception: framework trees (Next `app/`).

| Existing dir files | Action |
| --- | --- |
| 1 | Flatten; delete dir |
| 2 | Flatten unless framework requires |
| 3+ | Keep; barrel optional if ≥5 public exports |

Soft ceiling: ≤10 flat OK; 11–15 nest only with clear subdomain; 16+ nest by subdomain.
